    "reasoning": "Nitpicks: The agent did not include the England-and-Wales bunting value (not requested) and the output is formatted as a short list rather than, say, quoting JSON\u2014these do not affect correctness. The screenshots also often crop out the division header near the 2026 Scotland entries, but that is an evidence-capture limitation, not necessarily an agent mistake.\n\nCritical issues: None apparent. Screenshot 19 visibly contains 2026 event objects with exact titles and fields matching the agent\u2019s reported Scotland values: \u201c2nd January\u201d date 2026-01-02 bunting true; \u201cSummer bank holiday\u201d date 2026-08-03 bunting true; \u201cSt Andrew\u2019s Day\u201d date 2026-11-30 bunting true. For England and Wales, Screenshot 1 shows within the \u201cengland-and-wales\u201d section an event titled \u201cSummer bank holiday\u201d with date 2026-08-31, matching the agent\u2019s output. The action history shows the agent stayed on https://www.gov.uk/bank-holidays.json and merely enabled pretty-print and scrolled; there\u2019s no indication of using other sources or inferring dates from other years. The final output includes exactly the four requested deliverables and stops, aligning with the stopping condition.\n\nOverall, the agent delivered the exact requested 2026 dates and bunting values (for Scotland) and the requested 2026 England-and-Wales summer bank holiday date, sourced from the official GOV.UK JSON as required.",
